    "title": "Password cracking or brute-force tool",
    "desc": "An offline password cracker (john, hashcat) or an online brute-force tool (hydra, medusa, ncrack, patator) ran. On a security team's own box these are the job and fire constantly; on any other host they are a strong sign of a credential attack (MITRE T1110) - cracking a captured hash, or hammering a service login. That split is why the rule is optional: enable it where these tools should never run, leave it off on the pentest or CTF workstation that lives in them.",
